# The trust ledger (v0.11.0 bet 3; `cargo xtask check trust-ledger`).
#
# One row per (class, file): how many times the file SPELLS an input-narrowing
# assumption, and the artifact that justifies the figure. It counts spellings,
# not how much each one narrows; the gate prints the forms it cannot see.
#
# mode = equality     any change in any row fails -- growth AND an unrecorded
#                     shrink -- unless the same commit edits the row and names
#                     the artifact that justifies it.
# mode = shrink-only  set ONCE, in the first commit AFTER the v0.11.0 tag, with
#                     `baseline = <the sha the v0.11.0 tag points at>` (a commit
#                     cannot contain its own sha, so the baseline is the tagged
#                     commit, an ancestor). The gate requires the baseline to be a
#                     commit a `v*` tag points at, an ancestor of HEAD, AND the
#                     newest v* release (highest version) in HEAD's history, not
#                     counting a tag on HEAD itself -- so the ceiling only moves
#                     forward -- and reads the ledger AT it (git show), with paths
#                     carried through exact renames, as the ceiling: no row may
#                     exceed its baseline row and no new row may appear unless an
#                     `admit` row names it; the tree may not exceed this ledger; a
#                     shrink passes and is listed. After each new release tag the
#                     next commit is red until it moves the baseline to it (tags
#                     are the owner's) and folds the admits in (deletes them: the
#                     new baseline already carries the growth). Switching back to
#                     equality does not lift the ceiling: the last shrink-only
#                     ledger in history still names it. One `mode` and one
#                     `baseline` line only. The CI job checks out full history and
#                     tags for this.
#
# Admits: `admit <class> <path> +<N> @<baseline sha or v* tag> <#NNN |
# owner/repo#NNN> <reason>` -- one per item, N exactly the growth above the
# baseline row, written against the current baseline (an admit left in place
# when the baseline moves fails, and so does one already in the ledger AT that
# baseline: written before it, it admits nothing). Stale, oversized, duplicate or malformed
# admits fail. The gate checks the row is recorded against that baseline; it
# does not fetch the issue and cannot show that anyone reviewed or approved it.
#
# Pull requests (either mode; `cargo xtask check trust-ledger --base <rev>`,
# which the CI job runs with the merge-base on a pull_request): every row AND
# the tree are also held to the ledger AT the merge-base with the base branch
# (paths and admits carried through exact renames), or to the release
# ceiling's row where that is larger: a row shrunk after the tag may grow back
# up to the ceiling with no admit. A row may shrink; a larger count, a
# narrowed unwind bound or a row neither has fails unless the change RAISES
# the item's admit: the admit's +N minus the +N the merge-base ledger already
# admitted for that item (whatever its @) equals the growth exactly, and its @
# names a commit in the base branch's history (the merge-base or an ancestor:
# in equality mode the commit the change was written against; in shrink-only
# mode the release, as above). So an item's admit amount only grows while it
# stands: an admit carried over unchanged, or only re-pointed at another
# commit, grants nothing again. In equality mode with no ceiling an admit row
# grants nothing on push and is listed; the commit that sets the baseline
# deletes them with the fold. The `mode` and `baseline` lines are not involved.
#
# Rows: `<class> <path> <count> <ARTIFACT-ID>`; kani::unwind rows carry the
# sorted bounds before the ID, so a lowered bound is a change.
# Regenerate: `cargo xtask trust-ledger --write --id <ARTIFACT-ID>` (rows whose
# figure is unchanged keep their ID).
#
# Seeded 2026-11-20 at e85b7620 + this lane: 422 kani::assume in 22 files,
# 74 kani::unwind in 14, 135 external_body in 12, 2 assume_specification in 1,
# 74 Rocq Admitted in 3, 0 Lean sorry/axiom, 24 Rocq targets built with
# "-impredicative-set" (14 literals; plain/BUILD.bazel's one covers 11
# targets); denominators: 383 .rs, 13 .v, 8 .lean and 14 Bazel tracked
# files scanned (tools/xtask/ excluded). 496 #[kani::proof] attributes are in
# source -- a spelling count; kani-coverage prints how many sit in compiled
# roots (471, an upper bound on what CI runs: the root package's 25 in src/
# are never built).

mode = equality
baseline = none

